NhdST7789Spi.h adapts the upstream OLEDDisplay-compatible renderer, dirty
rectangle updates, scanline allocation and TFTColorRegion mapping. It retains
the ST7789Spi class name/API used by Meshtastic Screen, with explicit clock,
window offsets and panel MADCTL constructor arguments instead of ESP pin args.

Panel register values: Newhaven NHD-1.5-240240AF-CSXP product specification,
revision 1 (2026-03-11), printed pp. 11-12 (PDF pp. 12-13).
Local reference: parent hardware-reference/NHD-1.5-240240AF-CSXP.pdf.
Reset low/high: 250 ms each; sleep-out wait extended from 100 to 120 ms.
TE explicitly disabled. Initial address range follows the panel example
(columns 0..239, rows 0..319); rendering uses the specified 240x240 window
with explicit zero offsets, never upstream's centered 320x240 offsets.
Orientation retains the panel's BGR bit, toggling MY/MX for the BaseUI flip.
No power/backlight GPIO handling; display-off/on only blanks/unblanks output.
Buffers are allocated before dirty-state accounting, so allocation failure
does not discard an update. A hardware reset forces the next full refresh.
